### Step 1: Understand CSS variables

CSS variables allow you to define colors once and reuse them throughout your application.

For example:

```css
:root {
    --app-background: #f8fafc;
    --app-text: #1e293b;
}

body {
    background-color: var(--app-background);
    color: var(--app-text);
}
```

* `:root` selects the document's root element, normally the `<html>` element.

* `--app-background` is a custom CSS property.

* `var(--app-background)` reads the property's current value.

* `data-theme` is a custom HTML attribute we will use to identify the active theme.

When the value of a CSS variable changes, all styles that use it can update automatically.

