### Step 3: Understand the main properties

| Property                 | Purpose                                                                |
| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| --app-background         | Main page background                                                   |
| --app-text               | Default text color                                                     |
| --app-card               | Cards, panels, and content surfaces                                    |
| --app-border             | Borders and separators                                                 |
| --app-navbar             | Navigation bar background                                              |
| color-scheme             | Informs the browser about light or dark native controls                |
| transition               | Smoothly animates color changes                                        |
| :root[data-theme="dark"] | Applies dark variables when the HTML root has the dark theme attribute |

We also use some Bootstrap CSS variables in `.app-table` to make Bootstrap tables follow our custom colors.

Why use `data-theme`?

Our JavaScript will update the HTML element from:

```html
<html data-theme="light">
```

to:

```html
<html data-theme="dark">
```

The browser then applies the matching CSS variables without needing to rewrite every element's color individually.

Note: CSS `color-scheme` also affects browser-native elements such as scrollbars and some form controls. It does not automatically recolor every Bootstrap component; that is why we define explicit component styles.

